%N A401763 Square array A(n,k), n >= 1, k >= 1, read by antidiagonals: A(n,k) = h_n(r,s), the complete homogeneous symmetric polynomial of degree n in r and s; (r,s) is the k-th integer pair in lexicographic order subject to 1 <= s <= r: (1,1), (2,1), (2,2), (3,1), (3,2), (3,3), ...
%C A401763 For fixed k, A(n,k) = (r^(n+1) - s^(n+1))/(r-s) if r != s, and A(n,k) = (n+1)*r^n if r = s. The column generating function is 1/((1-r*x)*(1-s*x)), extending A(0,k) = 1.
%C A401763 The columns are Lucas sequences A(n,k) = U_(n+1)(P,Q), with P = r+s and Q = r*s, including the repeated-root cases. Their discriminants P^2 - 4*Q = (r-s)^2 are perfect squares.
%C A401763 Among the first 200 columns checked, 94 match existing OEIS sequences, including the first 79 consecutive columns. These matches span repeated-root sequences, repunits, geometric sums, and differences of powers.
%C A401763 See full identified list of matches in Links, and representative matches in Crossrefs.
%C A401763 From _Ruud H.G. van Tol_, Nov 05 2026: (Start)
%C A401763 The pair (r,s) of column k is r = A002024(k), s = A002260(k).
%C A401763 Each column is a rescaled coprime one: with g = gcd(r,s), A(n,k) = g^n*A(n,k'), where k' is the column of (r/g, s/g). So only the columns with gcd(r,s) = 1 are new; the columns with r = s are (n+1)*r^n, those with s | r are s^n*(q^(n+1) - 1)/(q - 1), q = r/s.
%C A401763 For gcd(r,s) = 1 each column is a strong divisibility sequence: gcd(A(a-1,k), A(b-1,k)) = A(gcd(a,b)-1,k), as gcd(r+s, r*s) = 1 (Lucas). It fails when gcd(r,s) > 1, e.g. for (2,2).
%C A401763 A(n,k) == (n+1)*r^n (mod r-s), as r == s (mod r-s): each column agrees with the repeated-root column (n+1)*r^n modulo r-s.
%C A401763 For (r,s) = (3,2), column 5 (A001047): under the Collatz map T(x) = x/2 (x even), (3x+1)/2 (x odd), an x == -1 (mod 2^n) takes n odd steps, and 2^n*T^n(x) = 3^n*x + A(n-1,5). (End)
%H A401763 Eddie Lin Rui, <a href="/A401763/b401763.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10011; the first 141 antidiagonals of the array</a>
%H A401763 Eddie Lin Rui, <a href="/A401763/a401763.txt">List of Identified OEIS Matches</a>.
%H A401763 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/CompleteHomogeneousSymmetricPolynomial.html">Complete Homogeneous Symmetric Polynomial</a>.
%H A401763 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/LucasSequence.html">Lucas Sequence</a>.
%F A401763 Let r be the smallest positive integer such that k <= r*(r+1)/2, and s = k - r*(r-1)/2.
%F A401763 A(n,k) = Sum_{i=0..n} r^(n-i)*s^i, for all positive integers n and k.
%F A401763 A(n,k) = (r+s)*A(n-1,k) - r*s*A(n-2,k), with A(0,k) = 1, A(-1,k) = 0. - _Ruud H.G. van Tol_, Nov 05 2026
